  "title": "Chapter 32: Indian Climate",
  "order": 218,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2p9r4id",
      "content": "The climate of India is described as a Tropical Monsoon Climate. It is primarily governed by seasonal reversal of winds known as the monsoon system. However, the Indian climate is not controlled by monsoon alone; several geographical, atmospheric and oceanic factors together shape the seasonal pattern of temperature and rainfall across the country."
    },
